<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal on course to meet euro targets - Guterres.</title>
<headline>Portugal on course to meet euro targets - Guterres.</headline>
<dateline>PONTA DELGADA, Portugal 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal and Spain want solidarity among European Union states in terms of attitudes to the planned single currency, Prime Minister Antonio Guterrres said.</p>
<p>He told a news conference Portugal was on course to meet targets to join the single currency, the euro.  </p>
<p>&quot;Solidarity is not divisible,&quot; Guterres said.</p>
<p>He added: &quot;I believe that Portugal's economic indicators show that Portugal is meeting Maastricht criteria consistently.&quot;</p>
<p>Guterres was speaking at the end of a two-day summit in the Azores with his Spanish counterpart Jose Maria Aznar.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
